message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below, and cite de Bruijn (1950) for the engine, Freire, Gonzalez-Riquelme, Munoz, Poblete and Salinas (arXiv:2610.27343) for the conditional statement, OpenAI's quasi-Riemann hypothesis preprint for the 7/8 half-plane, and Planat (arXiv:2609.37164) and Hakimoglu-Brown (arXiv:2610.12803) for the contraction inequalities used in version 2."
title: "Every real primitive Dirichlet L-function has de Bruijn-Newman constant at most 9/32: a kernel-checked proof in Lean 4"
authors:
